      "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nSequential partitioning currently counts lines using plain `open()` despite supporting gzip during the subsequent read. Its last-enumerated-line counter also remains undefined or stale for empty shards. Count with the same gzip-aware UTF-8 reader and `sum(1 for _ in fin)` so the partition size reflects actual documents.\n\nThis is an AI-assisted draft. Human author review and NVIDIA GPU/CI validation are pending.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: none; this is a narrowly scoped reproduced bug fix.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe actual compressed-input baseline raised UnicodeDecodeError. The added real-CLI matrix covers compressed/uncompressed input with/without an empty shard and verifies document order plus the first partition's exact size; three cases failed on baseline and all four pass with the fix. Expected file ordering follows the existing glob enumeration rather than imposing a new ordering policy.\n\n- Focused CPU validation: **4 passed** using actual production imports and generated fixtures; no production modules or functions are replaced by stubs.\n- Command: `/opt/cpu-review/bin/python -m pytest --confcutdir=tests/unit_tests/data tests/unit_tests/data/test_sequential_input_count.py -q`.\n- CPU environment: Linux container, Python 3.12, PyTorch 2.8 CPU, real Triton package for imports. `--confcutdir` excludes the parent suite's unrelated GPU/data fixtures; this is not the canonical NVIDIA development image or full distributed test run.\n- Repository `BASE_REF=main CHECK_ONLY=true SKIP_DOCS=false bash tools/autoformat.sh` completed successfully: Black, isort, Pylint and Ruff blocking checks passed.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests\n- [ ] I have added proper typing to my code\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation\n- [x] I have run the repository autoformatter\n\nNo GPU kernel is added or modified.\n",
